# Architecture (Idle Laboratory)

Local-first idle game. **No** Firebase / Supabase / remote DB clients.

```
UI → BLoC/Cubit → Service (RxDart) → Repository → LocalStorageDataSource → SharedPreferences
```

## Layers

- **Services** (`lib/features/*/domain/services/`): game logic, timers, `BehaviorSubject` / `foo$` streams, `@lazySingleton`. Heavy work lives here — not in BLoCs.
- **BLoCs**: thin stream subscribers; forward intents; extend `SafeBloc` when subscriptions call `add`. No SharedPreferences / JSON in BLoCs (except simple UI prefs via settings repo if already patterned that way).
- **Repositories**: persistence only (`guardAsync`, `StorageKeys`). No game rules.
- **Models**: Freezed; `BigNumber` + `lib/core/converters/`.

## `lib/core` placement

| Path | Contents |
|------|----------|
| `enums/` | Enum only |
| `extensions/` | Type helpers / formatters |
| `constants/` | Balance, keys, units |
| `utils/` | Pure math / algorithms |
| `widgets/` | Shared chrome |

## Persistence

- Keys only via `StorageKeys` — never ad-hoc prefs in UI.
- Lifetime stats survive prestige; run-scoped fields reset in the owning service.
- Debounced autosave on hot paths; immediate flush on prestige, lifecycle `paused`/`hidden`/`detached`, dispose.
- Playtime keeps running for `inactive` / `paused` / `hidden` while the process is alive; only end the segment on `detached` / dispose. Wall-clock catch-up on resume covers suspended timers.

## Tooling (ExFAT drive)

The repo sits on an ExFAT SSD: run Flutter commands as **`fflutter …`** (e.g. `fflutter test`, `fflutter gen-l10n`), not plain `flutter`. It cleans `._*` files and mounts the APFS build volume behind the symlinked `build/`, `Pods`, `Flutter/ephemeral`. `dart analyze` / `dart run build_runner …` work directly. Details: README → "Project on an ExFAT drive".

`ios/Runner.xcworkspace/contents.xcworkspacedata` (and any iOS / macOS project file the tooling rewrites with a `FlutterProjectsBuild` path) stays **locally modified on purpose**. Do not revert, stage or commit those rewrites. When reviewing diffs or PRs, flag them if they get staged or show up in a commit.

